Package: TrajChain
Type: Package
Title: Nonparametric Marker Trajectories Under Death and Delayed Entry
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pingbo", "Hu", , "pingbo.hu@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Estimates population-level biomarker trajectories from
    longitudinal cohort studies that enroll a cross-sectional sample of
    individuals at different ages and follow them over time. Deaths during
    follow-up cause informative censoring, and delayed entry induces left
    truncation that becomes informative in the presence of birth-cohort
    effects. Under a multiplicative latent-variable model, the common
    age-related shape of the trajectory is identified by kernel estimators of
    the ratio of the shape function at pairs of ages and is recovered over the
    whole age range by ratio chaining, without modeling survival, truncation
    or dropout beyond two conditional independence assumptions. Penalized
    extensions handle widely or unequally spaced visits. The package also
    estimates the unconditional mean trajectory and the composite
    birth-cohort-survivor bias, selects the bandwidth and the penalty by
    cross-validation, provides subject-level bootstrap standard errors and
    confidence bands, and simulates data from the designs studied in the
    accompanying paper by Hu, Wu, Zhao and Sun.
